<!--
    The cloud that does not know. A flat dash for a mouth — deliberately not a faint smile, which would read as "you're fine" about a mood nobody logged. This is what a new user sees, so it is the state that matters most.

    Four faces share one silhouette so they read as a single character changing expression rather
    than four unrelated icons. Only the eyes and mouth differ.

    **One path, fillType="evenOdd".** The eyes and mouth are holes in the cloud, not shapes drawn on
    top of it, so a single runtime tint colours the whole icon and the widget background shows
    through the face. Two-tone would need either a fixed palette that breaks in one theme or a
    duplicate set of drawables under drawable-night. Same lesson as the notification icon: let the
    shape carry the meaning.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="48dp"
    android:height="48dp"
    android:viewportWidth="48"
    android:viewportHeight="48">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M12,34 C6,34 6,25 13,24 C12,16 22,12 27,18 C33,13 42,18 40,25 C45,27 44,34 38,34 Z M18,25 a2,2 0 1,0 4,0 a2,2 0 1,0 -4,0 Z M29,25 a2,2 0 1,0 4,0 a2,2 0 1,0 -4,0 Z M21,30 h9 v1.8 h-9 Z" />
</vector>
